  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The maximum outcome in Lottery A is 2400 Euros, which occurs with 100% probability. The maximum outcome in Lottery B is 2500 Euros, which occurs with 33% probability. The reason compares the probabilities of the maximum outcomes: 100% for A and 33% for B. Since the reason prefers the lottery with the *lower* probability of the maximum outcome, it would prefer Lottery B (33%) over Lottery A (100%). The relevant information (maximum outcomes and their probabilities) is fully available in the problem description.",
